│  │     │  └─  49.9%      1.7M chars  4 files   src/alpha
│  │     ├─ locus: none sent — targetDiffs.additions
│  │     ├─ locus: 7.1M chars of target mass over 2 directories — targetDiffs.mutations
│  │     │  ├─  50.1%      3.5M chars  4 files   src/beta
│  │     │  └─  49.9%      3.5M chars  4 files   src/alpha
│  │     ├─ lever
│  │     │  ├─ edited files carry 100.0% of the target mass — their bodies and hunks
│  │     │  ├─ if the rubric grades this mass, partition it, so each partition fits, e.g.:
│  │     │  │  --partition 'beta=src/beta/**,.behavior/v2026_01_01.demo/**'
│  │     │  │  --partition 'alpha=src/alpha/**,.behavior/v2026_01_01.demo/**'
│  │     │  ├─ partition through vertical domains, never through horizontal layers: each partition holds a domain with its own tests (rule.forbid.horizontal-partitions)
│  │     │  ├─ add to each partition the files it must read to judge its own — shared types, domain objects; the overlap is computed, and a common file is graded once
│  │     │  ├─ preview the split before you spend: add --mode plan (under a guard: rhx route.guard.partition --for review --peer @all)
│  │     │  └─ if the rubric does not grade a subtree — a test corpus, a vendored or generated dir — cut it from the targets instead: --paths-wout '<subtree>/**' (a cut hides mass; a partition spreads it)
│  │     └─ hint
│  │        ├─ inspect .log/bhrain/review/<TIMESTAMP> to see what was matched
│  │        └─ inspect .log/bhrain/review/<TIMESTAMP> for token breakdown by file
│  │
│  └─
└─ passage blocked
   ├─ blocked by constraints
   └─ exit code: 2 ✋"
`;

